                <pb facs="0944" n="848" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.51/90: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schuyler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-30T21:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                                1921—9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 31—11:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Mexican Government has offered lend Salvadorean Government 3 million pesos as
                    act of friendliness, repayable from future loan. The President asks my opinion
                    as to whether he should accept in avoiding financial crisis. I was
                    noncommittal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
